      "content_hash": "fb28459057a6c052608e54fb7152ed00f67b4a17ecf4516c677fe642b3c0cf22",
      "heading": "3. [DLID]の解決",
      "position": 3,
      "section_id": "DLID-m0xegzfyhc3k"
    }
  ],
  "summary": [
    "Pre-search check distinguishes no rebuild needed, rebuild needed, and undeterminable, and asks the user to choose rebuild-then-search or search the existing version",
    "Rebuild scale is shown as counts only, with details and the target specification file written under the work directory",
    "Undeterminable results are treated as failures and never read as up to date; search stops with the cause reported",
    "Each result candidate carries document ID, recorded path, relevance, reason, optional sections, and ToC key, version and freshness",
    "A script fixes the ToC and partitions documents among at most 10 read-only search AI workers; every document is read one at a time",
    "Workers answer with yes, maybe or no only, never see or write IDs, and name sections by heading that the script resolves",
    "Answers are validated on receipt; unmatched headings are rejected with candidates, and a search with unanswered documents fails",
    "Result order follows assignment order, not relevance, and maybe is never promoted to yes",
    "resolve-dlid resolves DLIDs from recorded state and the recorded path file, returning resolved, not at recorded path, or no record, with content hash",
    "Search and resolution never write to the ToC, management state, or target documents"
  ],
